{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -NoProfile -Command \"rg -n '\"'^'\"' INTENT.md after/segmented_download.rs | Select-Object -First 325\"","aggregated_output":"INTENT.md:1:# INTENT: `segmented_download.rs` (VNovel Library)\r\nINTENT.md:2:\r\nINTENT.md:3:Owner: the user (the app's author). Draft recovered from the code, the module's four commits\r\nINTENT.md:4:(d39e979, d3a2664, d4d4666, 369aed7), `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §2/§4 and the only caller\r\nINTENT.md:5:(`dist_host.rs` `download_dist_files`). Changes need the owner's approval.\r\nINTENT.md:6:\r\nINTENT.md:7:## Purpose\r\nINTENT.md:8:The file host's web page (driven by `dist_host.rs` in a hidden WebView2) yields a final, signed file\r\nINTENT.md:9:URL plus cookies. This module turns that URL into a complete file in the VN folder: fast on hosts\r\nINTENT.md:10:that throttle each connection, resumable after cancel or an app restart, and never leaving a\r\nINTENT.md:11:silently corrupted file. Real files are large (the module was validated on a 4.22 GiB file by\r\nINTENT.md:12:SHA-256).\r\nINTENT.md:13:\r\nINTENT.md:14:## Public contract (the caller must keep compiling unchanged)\r\nINTENT.md:15:```rust\r\nINTENT.md:16:pub struct DownloadRequest { pub url: String, pub destination: PathBuf,\r\nINTENT.md:17:                             pub cookie_header: Option<String>, pub referer: Option<String> }\r\nINTENT.md:18:pub enum DownloadMode { Segmented, Single }          // Serialize, lowercase (\"segmented\"/\"single\")\r\nINTENT.md:19:pub struct DownloadProgress { pub received: u64, pub total: Option<u64>, pub mode: DownloadMode }\r\nINTENT.md:20:pub fn register_cancel(token: &str) -> Arc<AtomicBool>\r\nINTENT.md:21:pub fn request_cancel(token: &str) -> bool           // true if the token was registered\r\nINTENT.md:22:pub fn clear_cancel(token: &str)\r\nINTENT.md:23:pub async fn download<F: Fn(DownloadProgress) + Send + Sync + 'static>(\r\nINTENT.md:24:    request: DownloadRequest, cancel: Arc<AtomicBool>, on_progress: F,\r\nINTENT.md:25:) -> Result<Option<PathBuf>, String>                 // Some(path) done, None cancelled, Err failed\r\nINTENT.md:26:```\r\nINTENT.md:27:`DownloadMode`, `DownloadProgress` and `DownloadRequest` may derive more traits, never fewer\r\nINTENT.md:28:(`Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize` as today).\r\nINTENT.md:29:\r\nINTENT.md:30:## Intents\r\nINTENT.md:31:| ID | Intent |\r\nINTENT.md:32:|---|---|\r\nINTENT.md:33:| D1 | The destination file is byte-identical to what the server holds (any size, including 0 bytes). On success nothing else is left in the folder. The destination appears only when complete |\r\nINTENT.md:34:| D2 | First request: `Range: bytes=0-0`. A 206 with a known total ??parallel download. Anything else usable (200, unknown total `*`) ??one plain stream. An HTTP error ??`Err`, no file |\r\nINTENT.md:35:| D3 | Parallel download uses several connections, **never more than 8** (hosts are shared; the user's other traffic matters) |\r\nINTENT.md:36:| D4 | Cancel or app restart keeps resume state next to the destination. The next `download` of the same URL into the same destination fetches only what is missing (up to ~1 MiB per connection may be refetched). State left by a different file (different size) is discarded |\r\nINTENT.md:37:| D5 | Never a wrong final file: a 206 whose `Content-Range` does not start where it was asked, a body longer than asked, a short body, or damaged resume state must lead to a retry, a re-download or `Err`, never to a completed file with wrong bytes |\r\nINTENT.md:38:| D6 | Transient network failures are retried (about 4 tries per piece, short growing backoff), **the probe included**; a persistent failure ends in `Err` within seconds. **A server that keeps the connection open but sends nothing for 30 s counts as a failure** (so a fully stalled server ends in `Err` within about 2 minutes). The single stream is not retried automatically: it would restart from byte 0 |\r\nINTENT.md:39:| D7 | Cancellation is prompt **(within about 1 s, even while the server sends nothing)**: `download` returns `Ok(None)`, keeps resume state, and the destination does not appear. Tokens: `register_cancel` makes a fresh flag, `request_cancel` sets it, `clear_cancel` forgets it |\r\nINTENT.md:40:| D8 | Progress: `received` never goes backwards, `total` is the full size when known, `mode` tells which path is used; at most about 4 events per second; the last event reports `received == total` |\r\nINTENT.md:41:| D9 | Every request sends `Accept-Encoding: identity` (byte offsets must be file offsets), the cookie and referer when non-empty, and a desktop Chrome user agent; up to 10 redirects; 20 s connect timeout |\r\nINTENT.md:42:| D10 | Errors are human-readable Korean strings (the caller shows them as they are) |\r\nINTENT.md:43:| P1 | No regression vs. the start on: 80 MB with a per-connection limit, 80 MB where some connections are slow, 512 MB unthrottled (`run.sh` bench) |\r\nINTENT.md:44:\r\nINTENT.md:45:## Revision 1 (owner-approved, after the W4 skeptic rounds)\r\nINTENT.md:46:- D6/D7 above: stall detection (30 s without data), probe retries, cancel within ~1 s during a stall.\r\nINTENT.md:47:- Deliberately not done: automatic single-stream retry (restarts from 0), fsync of data/state (power-loss\r\nINTENT.md:48:  durability; cost on external HDDs; disclosed in the module header `Weak:`).\r\nINTENT.md:49:- Transition: the resume-state format changed (one text `.download.state` instead of three sidecars). No\r\nINTENT.md:50:  migration code: before switching versions, finish or remove paused downloads in the old app. A leftover\r\nINTENT.md:51:  old download restarts from 0 and leaves an orphan `.download.json`; it never produces a wrong file.\r\nINTENT.md:52:\r\nINTENT.md:53:## Scale and assumptions\r\nINTENT.md:54:- Files from a few bytes to tens of GB. One download at a time (the caller's queue is sequential).\r\nINTENT.md:55:- The same URL serves the same bytes while a download is in progress or paused.\r\nINTENT.md:56:\r\nINTENT.md:57:## Non-goals\r\nINTENT.md:58:- Resuming the single-stream path (servers without Range cannot resume).\r\nINTENT.md:59:- Checksums, ETag/Last-Modified validation, bandwidth limiting, HTTP/2 tuning, multiple\r\nINTENT.md:60:  simultaneous downloads, a configurable number of connections.\r\nINTENT.md:61:- Keeping the current sidecar file names or format (only this module reads them).\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:1://! Intent: 최종 ?�일 URL??최�? 8�??�결�??�눠 받아 ?�개 가?�하�??�성?�다. ?�못??바이?�로 ?�난 ?�일?� 만들지 ?�는??D1-D10).\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:2://! Data: ?��? 구간 목록 `[start,end)`(미배??`todo` + ?�결�?진행 �?`slots`)???��??? ?�개 ?�태????목록???��? 고정 ?�기 ?�스??sidecar ??개다(FNV ??+ ???�식).\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:3://! Assumes: 같�? URL?� 진행/중단 ?�안 같�? 바이?��? 준???�기�?검�?. ?�버??`Content-Range`(?�작·총량)�?지?�다. ?�일 ?�기??짧아??async ?�에??블로?�해???�다.\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:4://! Weak: 같�? ?�기???�른 ?�일?� �??�아챈다(?�인??. fsync�??��? ?�아 ?�전 ???�태가 ?�이?�보???�설 ???�다. ?�일 ?�트림�? ?�개???�동 ?�시?�도 ?�다(0부???�시 받게 ?��?�?. ?�일 ?�기가 ?�래 멈추�?그동??비동�??�업?��? 붙잡?�다.\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:5://! Cost: �?��마다 mutex ?�나(기록+진행 갱신), 1 MiB마다 ?�태 ?�일 ?�자�???��?�기. ?�린 ?�결?� ?�에???��? 구간??�??�결???�겨(steal) 보완?�되 버려지???�송 �?바이?��? ?�다.\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:6:\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:7:use reqwest::header::{ACCEPT_ENCODING, CONTENT_RANGE, COOKIE, RANGE, REFERER};\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:8:use reqwest::{Client, RequestBuilder, StatusCode};\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:9:use serde::Serialize;\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:10:use std::collections::HashMap;\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:11:use std::io::{Seek, SeekFrom, Write};\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:12:use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\r\nafter/segmented_download.rs:13:use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicBool, Ordering};\r\nafter